This is a deliberate, explicit statement of the project's current terms, not a
placeholder. No licence to use, copy, modify or distribute this software is
granted. Until an open licence is issued, the only rights anyone has in this
repository are the ones GitHub's Terms of Service give every user of a public
repository (to view it and to fork it within GitHub), plus whatever applies by
law independently of a licence.

Why this file says that
-----------------------
The repository has been public with no LICENSE, no `license` field in
pyproject.toml and no licence classifier, while README.md said a licence was
coming "shortly" and CONTRIBUTING.md asked contributors to pre-agree to it. A
promise is not a grant, and the absence of a licence file is not neutral — it
reads as an oversight when it is in fact the strictest possible term. Saying
"all rights reserved" out loud is the honest version of the state the project
is already in.

What is being pursued
---------------------
An open licence, through SLAC's Office of Technology Licensing. Apache-2.0 is
the recommendation on the table: it is the usual outcome for SLAC-affiliated
scientific Python, its patent and NOTICE clauses are what a national-lab
technology-transfer office asks for, and it is compatible with every inbound
licence this repository depends on (see THIRD_PARTY.md — MIT for three.js,
gif.js, h5wasm and plotly; BSD-3-Clause for numpy, scipy and jax; CC0 for the
matplotlib colormap stops).

Replacing this file with that licence is a decision for the project owner and
SLAC OTL, not for whoever is editing the tree. Until then:

  * Do not publish a wheel or an sdist to PyPI. An unlicensed artefact on PyPI
    is worse than no artefact.
  * Do not add a `license` field or a `License ::` classifier claiming terms
    that have not been granted.
  * Third-party material vendored here keeps its own terms, which are not
    affected by this file. THIRD_PARTY.md is the inventory.

Third-party notices
-------------------
See THIRD_PARTY.md and LICENSES/. Several third-party files in this repository
arrived with no licence text at all; THIRD_PARTY.md names each one and says
what has to happen about it.
